{"id":"mahabharata-3-198","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":198,"title":"अष्टनवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 198 · The righteous hunter of Mithila","summary":{"en":"Kaushika finds the dharmavyadha, the righteous meat-seller, in his shop in Mithila; the man already knows who sent him. He takes Kaushika home and teaches him at length the duties of the classes, truthfulness, restraint and the conduct of the good.","kn":"ಕೌಶಿಕನು ಮಿಥಿಲೆಯ ಅಂಗಡಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಧರ್ಮವ್ಯಾಧನನ್ನು ಕಾಣುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವನನ್ನು ಯಾರು ಕಳುಹಿಸಿದರೆಂದು ಅವನಿಗೆ ಮೊದಲೇ ತಿಳಿದಿದೆ. ಕೌಶಿಕನನ್ನು ಮನೆಗೆ ಕರೆದೊಯ್ದು ವರ್ಣಧರ್ಮ, ಸತ್ಯ, ಸಂಯಮ, ಶಿಷ್ಟಾಚಾರಗಳನ್ನು ವಿಸ್ತಾರವಾಗಿ ಉಪದೇಶಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"कौशिक मिथिला में अपनी दुकान पर धर्मव्याध को पाते हैं; वह पहले से जानता है कि उन्हें किसने भेजा है। वह कौशिक को घर ले जाकर वर्णधर्म, सत्य, संयम और सज्जनों के आचरण का विस्तार से उपदेश देता है।","te":"కౌశికుడు మిథిలలో దుకాణంలో ధర్మవ్యాధుని కలుస్తాడు; తనను ఎవరు పంపారో అతనికి ముందే తెలుసు. కౌశికుని ఇంటికి తీసుకువెళ్లి వర్ణధర్మాలు, సత్యం, సంయమం, శిష్టాచారాలను విస్తారంగా ఉపదేశిస్తాడు.","ta":"கௌஶிகர் மிதிலையில் கடையில் தர்மவ்யாதனைக் காண்கிறார்; அவரை யார் அனுப்பினார் என்று அவனுக்கு முன்பே தெரிந்திருக்கிறது. அவன் கௌஶிகரை வீட்டுக்கு அழைத்துச் சென்று வர்ணக் கடமைகள், உண்மை, அடக்கம், சான்றோர் ஒழுக்கம் ஆகியவற்றை விரிவாக உபதேசிக்கிறான்.","ml":"മിഥിലയിലെ കടയിൽ, ധർമ്മവ്യാധനായ മാംസവ്യാപാരിയെ കൗശികൻ കണ്ടെത്തുന്നു; തന്നെ ആരാണ് അയച്ചതെന്ന് അയാൾക്ക് മുമ്പേ അറിയാം. അയാൾ കൗശികനെ വീട്ടിലേക്ക് കൊണ്ടുപോയി വർണ്ണങ്ങളുടെ കർത്തവ്യങ്ങൾ, സത്യം, സംയമനം, സജ്ജനങ്ങളുടെ നടപടികൾ എന്നിവ വിശദമായി പഠിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.198; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"मार्कण्डेयसमास्यापर्व","titleEn":"Markandeyasamasya Parva (Session with Markandeya)","verses":[{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"चिन्तयित्वा तदाश्चर्यं स्त्रिया प्रोक्तमशेषतः ।\nविनिन्दन्स द्विजोऽऽत्मानमागस्कृत इवाबभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pondering the wonder that the woman had told him in full, the brahmin reproached himself and seemed like one who had committed a fault."}},{"n":2,"text":"चिन्तयानः स धर्मस्य सूक्ष्मां गतिमथाब्रवीत् ।\nश्रद्दधानेन भाव्यं वै गच्छामि मिथिलामहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking of the subtle course of dharma, he said, \"One ought to have faith. I will go to Mithila."}},{"n":3,"text":"कृतात्मा धर्मवित्तस्यां व्याधो निवसते किल ।\nतं गच्छाम्यहमद्यैव धर्मं प्रष्टुं तपोधनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A hunter of cultivated soul who knows dharma lives there, they say. I will go to him this very day to ask about dharma, that man rich in austerity.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"इति संचिन्त्य मनसा श्रद्दधानः स्त्रिया वचः ।\nबलाकाप्रत्ययेनासौ धर्म्यैश्च वचनैः शुभैः ।\nसंप्रतस्थे स मिथिलां कौतूहलसमन्वितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thinking so in his mind, having faith in the woman's words, convinced by the matter of the crane and by her righteous, good speech, he set out for Mithila, full of curiosity."}},{"n":5,"text":"अतिक्रामन्नरण्यानि ग्रामांश्च नगराणि च ।\nततो जगाम मिथिलां जनकेन सुरक्षिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crossing forests, villages and towns, he came to Mithila, well guarded by Janaka,"}},{"n":6,"text":"धर्मसेतुसमाकीर्णां यज्ञोत्सववतीं शुभाम् ।\nगोपुराट्टालकवतीं गृहप्राकारशोभिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"a lovely city crowded with causeways of dharma, with sacrifices and festivals, with gate-towers and watchtowers, adorned with house walls."}},{"n":7,"text":"प्रविश्य स पुरीं रम्यां विमानैर्बहुभिर्वृताम् ।\nपण्यैश्च बहुभिर्युक्तां सुविभक्तमहापथाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He entered that charming city, surrounded by many palaces, full of much merchandise, with well-divided great roads,"}},{"n":8,"text":"अश्वै रथैस्तथा नागैर्यानैश्च बहुभिर्वृताम् ।\nहृष्टपुष्टजनाकीर्णां नित्योत्सवसमाकुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"thronged with horses, chariots, elephants and many vehicles, filled with cheerful, well-fed people and busy with constant festivals."}},{"n":9,"text":"सोऽपश्यद्बहुवृत्तान्तां ब्राह्मणः समतिक्रमन् ।\nधर्मव्याधमपृच्छच्च स चास्य कथितो द्विजैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he passed through, the brahmin saw much going on, and he asked after the dharma-hunter, and the brahmins told him where he was."}},{"n":10,"text":"अपश्यत्तत्र गत्वा तं सूनामध्ये व्यवस्थितम् ।\nमार्गमाहिषमांसानि विक्रीणन्तं तपस्विनम् ।\nआकुलत्वात्तु क्रेतॄणामेकान्ते संस्थितो द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going there he saw the ascetic seated amid the slaughterhouse, selling the meat of deer and buffalo; and because of the press of buyers the brahmin stayed to one side."}},{"n":11,"text":"स तु ज्ञात्वा द्विजं प्राप्तं सहसा संभ्रमोत्थितः ।\nआजगाम यतो विप्रः स्थित एकान्त आसने ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hunter, knowing a brahmin had come, rose suddenly in haste and came to where the brahmin sat in a secluded seat."}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"अभिवादये त्वा भगवन्स्वागतं ते द्विजोत्तम ।\nअहं व्याधस्तु भद्रं ते किं करोमि प्रशाधि माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I greet you, revered one; welcome, best of brahmins. I am a hunter. May you be well. What shall I do? Command me."}},{"n":13,"text":"एकपत्न्या यदुक्तोऽसि गच्छ त्वं मिथिलामिति ।\nजानाम्येतदहं सर्वं यदर्थं त्वमिहागतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know all that for which you have come here: that you were told by the wife of one husband to go to Mithila."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु तस्य तद्वाक्यं स विप्रो भृशहर्षितः ।\nद्वितीयमिदमाश्चर्यमित्यचिन्तयत द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, the brahmin was greatly delighted and thought, \"This is a second wonder.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"अदेशस्थं हि ते स्थानमिति व्याधोऽब्रवीद्द्विजम् ।\nगृहं गच्छाव भगवन्यदि रोचयसेऽनघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"This is not a fitting place for you,\" the hunter said to the brahmin. \"Let us go to my house, revered one, if you like, blameless one.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"बाढमित्येव संहृष्टो विप्रो वचनमब्रवीत् ।\nअग्रतस्तु द्विजं कृत्वा स जगाम गृहान्प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Very well,\" said the brahmin, delighted, and, putting the brahmin ahead, he went toward his house."}},{"n":17,"text":"प्रविश्य च गृहं रम्यमासनेनाभिपूजितः ।\nपाद्यमाचमनीयं च प्रतिगृह्य द्विजोत्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering the lovely house, honoured with a seat, the best of brahmins accepted water for his feet and for rinsing his mouth."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः सुखोपविष्टस्तं व्याधं वचनमब्रवीत् ।\nकर्मैतद्वै न सदृशं भवतः प्रतिभाति मे ।\nअनुतप्ये भृशं तात तव घोरेण कर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seated comfortably, he said to the hunter, \"This work does not seem fitting for you; I am greatly distressed, dear one, by your cruel occupation.\""}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"कुलोचितमिदं कर्म पितृपैतामहं मम ।\nवर्तमानस्य मे धर्मे स्वे मन्युं मा कृथा द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"This work is proper to my family, handed down from my father and grandfather. Do not be angry, brahmin, at me living by my own dharma."}},{"n":20,"text":"धात्रा तु विहितं पूर्वं कर्म स्वं पालयाम्यहम् ।\nप्रयत्नाच्च गुरू वृद्धौ शुश्रूषेऽहं द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I follow my own work, as ordained by the creator long ago, and I carefully serve my elderly parents, best of brahmins."}},{"n":21,"text":"सत्यं वदे नाभ्यसूये यथाशक्ति ददामि च ।\nदेवतातिथिभृत्यानामवशिष्टेन वर्तये ॥","meaning":{"en":"I speak truth, I am not envious, I give as far as I can, and I live on what remains after the gods, guests and dependants."}},{"n":22,"text":"न कुत्सयाम्यहं किंचिन्न गर्हे बलवत्तरम् ।\nकृतमन्वेति कर्तारं पुरा कर्म द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not slander anyone and do not blame those stronger than I; the deed done earlier follows the doer, best of brahmins."}},{"n":23,"text":"कृषिगोरक्ष्यवाणिज्यमिह लोकस्य जीवनम् ।\nदण्डनीतिस्त्रयी विद्या तेन लोका भवन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Farming, cattle-keeping and trade are this world's livelihood; the science of punishment, and the triple Veda, keep the world going."}},{"n":24,"text":"कर्म शूद्रे कृषिर्वैश्ये संग्रामः क्षत्रिये स्मृतः ।\nब्रह्मचर्यं तपो मन्त्राः सत्यं च ब्राह्मणे सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Work for the servant is said to be farming, for the merchant trade, for the warrior war; for the brahmin always celibacy, austerity, mantras and truth."}},{"n":25,"text":"राजा प्रशास्ति धर्मेण स्वकर्मनिरताः प्रजाः ।\nविकर्माणश्च ये केचित्तान्युनक्ति स्वकर्मसु ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king rules by dharma, and subjects are devoted to their own work; those who do forbidden work, he yokes back to their own duties."}},{"n":26,"text":"भेतव्यं हि सदा राज्ञां प्रजानामधिपा हि ते ।\nमारयन्ति विकर्मस्थं लुब्धा मृगमिवेषुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings must always be feared, for they are lords of the people; greedy, they kill one who does wrong with arrows as one hunts a deer."}},{"n":27,"text":"जनकस्येह विप्रर्षे विकर्मस्थो न विद्यते ।\nस्वकर्मनिरता वर्णाश्चत्वारोऽपि द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"In Janaka's realm, brahmin sage, there is no one who does forbidden work; all four classes, best of brahmins, are devoted to their own work."}},{"n":28,"text":"स एष जनको राजा दुर्वृत्तमपि चेत्सुतम् ।\nदण्ड्यं दण्डे निक्षिपति तथा न ग्लाति धार्मिकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This King Janaka, even if his own son behaves badly, imposes the punishment due, and he does not tire of dharma."}},{"n":29,"text":"सुयुक्तचारो नृपतिः सर्वं धर्मेण पश्यति ।\nश्रीश्च राज्यं च दण्डश्च क्षत्रियाणां द्विजोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"A king who has employed good spies sees everything in accordance with dharma. Fortune, kingdom and punishment belong to warriors, best of brahmins."}},{"n":30,"text":"राजानो हि स्वधर्मेण श्रियमिच्छन्ति भूयसीम् ।\nसर्वेषामेव वर्णानां त्राता राजा भवत्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings by their own dharma desire greater fortune; the king is the protector of all classes."}},{"n":31,"text":"परेण हि हतान्ब्रह्मन्वराहमहिषानहम् ।\nन स्वयं हन्मि विप्रर्षे विक्रीणामि सदा त्वहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin, I do not kill the boars and buffalo myself; they are killed by others, and I only sell them, brahmin sage."}},{"n":32,"text":"न भक्षयामि मांसानि ऋतुगामी तथा ह्यहम् ।\nसदोपवासी च तथा नक्तभोजी तथा द्विज ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not eat meat; I approach my wife only in season; I always fast, and I eat only at night, brahmin."}},{"n":33,"text":"अशीलश्चापि पुरुषो भूत्वा भवति शीलवान् ।\nप्राणिहिंसारतश्चापि भवते धार्मिकः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even a man without good character can become virtuous, and one given to killing creatures can become righteous again."}},{"n":34,"text":"व्यभिचारान्नरेन्द्राणां धर्मः संकीर्यते महान् ।\nअधर्मो वर्धते चापि संकीर्यन्ते तथा प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Through the misconduct of kings great dharma is confused; unrighteousness grows and the people are mixed up."}},{"n":35,"text":"उरुण्डा वामनाः कुब्जाः स्थूलशीर्षास्तथैव च ।\nक्लीबाश्चान्धाश्च जायन्ते बधिरा लम्बचूचुकाः ।\nपार्थिवानामधर्मत्वात्प्रजानामभवः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"People are born crippled, dwarfish, hunchbacked, big-headed, impotent, blind, deaf and with drooping nipples; through kings' unrighteousness there is always ruin for their subjects."}},{"n":36,"text":"स एष राजा जनकः सर्वं धर्मेण पश्यति ।\nअनुगृह्णन्प्रजाः सर्वाः स्वधर्मनिरताः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"This King Janaka sees all by dharma, favouring all his subjects, who are always devoted to their own duties."}},{"n":37,"text":"ये चैव मां प्रशंसन्ति ये च निन्दन्ति मानवाः ।\nसर्वान्सुपरिणीतेन कर्मणा तोषयाम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether people praise me or blame me, I satisfy them all by well-done work."}},{"n":38,"text":"ये जीवन्ति स्वधर्मेण संभुञ्जन्ते च पार्थिवाः ।\nन किंचिदुपजीवन्ति दक्षा उत्थानशीलिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kings eat and enjoy what they live on by their own dharma; capable and energetic men do not live off others at all."}},{"n":39,"text":"शक्त्यान्नदानं सततं तितिक्षा धर्मनित्यता ।\nयथार्हं प्रतिपूजा च सर्वभूतेषु वै दया ।\nत्यागान्नान्यत्र मर्त्यानां गुणास्तिष्ठन्ति पूरुषे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Giving food as one is able, constant forbearance, steadiness in dharma, due honour to others and compassion to all beings: apart from renunciation, these are the qualities that stay in a mortal man."}},{"n":40,"text":"मृषावादं परिहरेत्कुर्यात्प्रियमयाचितः ।\nन च कामान्न संरम्भान्न द्वेषाद्धर्ममुत्सृजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should avoid falsehood, do what is kind unasked, and not abandon dharma out of desire, rage or hatred."}},{"n":41,"text":"प्रिये नातिभृशं हृष्येदप्रिये न च संज्वरेत् ।\nन मुह्येदर्थकृच्छ्रेषु न च धर्मं परित्यजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not rejoice too much at the pleasant nor burn at the unpleasant, not be bewildered in financial hardship, nor give up dharma."}},{"n":42,"text":"कर्म चेत्किंचिदन्यत्स्यादितरन्न समाचरेत् ।\nयत्कल्याणमभिध्यायेत्तत्रात्मानं नियोजयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If there are other work to do, one should not do another's; one should set oneself to whatever one considers good."}},{"n":43,"text":"न पापं प्रति पापः स्यात्साधुरेव सदा भवेत् ।\nआत्मनैव हतः पापो यः पापं कर्तुमिच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"One should not answer evil with evil but always be good; the sinner who wishes to commit sin is killed by himself."}},{"n":44,"text":"कर्म चैतदसाधूनां वृजिनानामसाधुवत् ।\nन धर्मोऽस्तीति मन्वानाः शुचीनवहसन्ति ये ।\nअश्रद्दधाना धर्मस्य ते नश्यन्ति न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This kind of deed belongs to the wicked and the crooked; those who think \"there is no dharma\" and mock the pure, having no faith in dharma, are surely ruined."}},{"n":45,"text":"महादृतिरिवाध्मातः पापो भवति नित्यदा ।\nमूढानामवलिप्तानामसारं भाषितं भवेत् ।\nदर्शयत्यन्तरात्मानं दिवा रूपमिवांशुमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The evil man, always puffed up like a great leather bag, speaks hollow words among the foolish and the proud; he shows his inner self as the sun shows form by day."}},{"n":46,"text":"न लोके राजते मूर्खः केवलात्मप्रशंसया ।\nअपि चेह मृजा हीनः कृतविद्यः प्रकाशते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fool does not shine in the world through mere self-praise, while one without polish but with learning shines here."}},{"n":47,"text":"अब्रुवन्कस्यचिन्निन्दामात्मपूजामवर्णयन् ।\nन कश्चिद्गुणसंपन्नः प्रकाशो भुवि दृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who speaks of no one's faults and does not describe his own praise: no man of such merit is seen so evident on earth."}},{"n":48,"text":"विकर्मणा तप्यमानः पापाद्विपरिमुच्यते ।\nनैतत्कुर्यां पुनरिति द्वितीयात्परिमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"One tormented by his wrong deed is freed from the sin; resolving \"I will not do this again\", he is freed from the second."}},{"n":49,"text":"कर्मणा येन तेनेह पापाद्द्विजवरोत्तम ।\nएवं श्रुतिरियं ब्रह्मन्धर्मेषु परिदृश्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"By whatever act, best of the best of brahmins, one is freed here from sin: so this scriptural teaching is seen in the dharmas."}},{"n":50,"text":"पापान्यबुद्ध्वेह पुरा कृतानि\nप्राग्धर्मशीलो विनिहन्ति पश्चात् ।\nधर्मो ब्रह्मन्नुदते पूरुषाणां\nयत्कुर्वते पापमिह प्रमादात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not knowing the sins done earlier in this life, a man who was earlier of righteous nature later destroys them; dharma, brahmin, drives off the evil that men do here through carelessness."}},{"n":51,"text":"पापं कृत्वा हि मन्येत नाहमस्मीति पूरुषः ।\nचिकीर्षेदेव कल्याणं श्रद्दधानोऽनसूयकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having done a sin, a man should think \"I am not that\"; having faith and without envy, he should seek only good."}},{"n":52,"text":"वसनस्येव छिद्राणि साधूनां विवृणोति यः ।\nपापं चेत्पुरुषः कृत्वा कल्याणमभिपद्यते ।\nमुच्यते सर्वपापेभ्यो महाभ्रैरिव चन्द्रमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who exposes the faults of the good like holes in a cloth: but if a man, having sinned, turns to good, he is freed from all sins like the moon from great clouds."}},{"n":53,"text":"यथादित्यः समुद्यन्वै तमः सर्वं व्यपोहति ।\nएवं कल्याणमातिष्ठन्सर्वपापैः प्रमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the rising sun drives away all darkness, so one who practises good is freed from all sins."}},{"n":54,"text":"पापानां विद्ध्यधिष्ठानं लोभमेव द्विजोत्तम ।\nलुब्धाः पापं व्यवस्यन्ति नरा नातिबहुश्रुताः ।\nअधर्मा धर्मरूपेण तृणैः कूपा इवावृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know greed to be the seat of sins, best of brahmins; greedy men, not very learned, resolve upon sin; the unrighteous, in the form of righteousness, are like wells covered by grass."}},{"n":55,"text":"तेषां दमः पवित्राणि प्रलापा धर्मसंश्रिताः ।\nसर्वं हि विद्यते तेषु शिष्टाचारः सुदुर्लभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their self-restraint, purifications and talk rely on dharma; everything is found in them, but the conduct of the good is very hard to find."}},{"text":"मार्कण्डेय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Markandeya said:"}},{"n":56,"text":"स तु विप्रो महाप्राज्ञो धर्मव्याधमपृच्छत ।\nशिष्टाचारं कथमहं विद्यामिति नरोत्तम ।\nएतन्महामते व्याध प्रब्रवीहि यथातथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That very wise brahmin then asked the dharma-hunter, \"Best of men, how am I to know the conduct of the good? Tell me this exactly, high-minded hunter.\""}},{"text":"व्याध उवाच","meaning":{"en":"The hunter said:"}},{"n":57,"text":"यज्ञो दानं तपो वेदाः सत्यं च द्विजसत्तम ।\nपञ्चैतानि पवित्राणि शिष्टाचारेषु नित्यदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sacrifice, giving, austerity, the Vedas and truth, best of brahmins: these five are always the purifiers in the conduct of the good."}},{"n":58,"text":"कामक्रोधौ वशे कृत्वा दम्भं लोभमनार्जवम् ।\nधर्म इत्येव संतुष्टास्ते शिष्टाः शिष्टसंमताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who have mastered desire and anger, and arrogance, greed and crookedness, and are content simply with dharma, are the good, approved by the good."}},{"n":59,"text":"न तेषां विद्यतेऽवृत्तं यज्ञस्वाध्यायशीलिनाम् ।\nआचारपालनं चैव द्वितीयं शिष्टलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In them, devoted to sacrifice and study, there is no misconduct; and keeping to proper conduct is the second mark of the good."}},{"n":60,"text":"गुरुशुश्रूषणं सत्यमक्रोधो दानमेव च ।\nएतच्चतुष्टयं ब्रह्मञ्शिष्टाचारेषु नित्यदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Serving the teacher, truth, freedom from anger, and giving: these four, brahmin, are always found in the conduct of the good."}},{"n":61,"text":"शिष्टाचारे मनः कृत्वा प्रतिष्ठाप्य च सर्वशः ।\nयामयं लभते तुष्टिं सा न शक्या ह्यतोऽन्यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having set the mind on the conduct of the good and fixed it there entirely, the contentment one gains from it cannot be had otherwise."}},{"n":62,"text":"वेदस्योपनिषत्सत्यं सत्यस्योपनिषद्दमः ।\nदमस्योपनिषत्त्यागः शिष्टाचारेषु नित्यदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The inner meaning of the Veda is truth, the inner meaning of truth is self-restraint, and the inner meaning of self-restraint is renunciation; these are always in the conduct of the good."}},{"n":63,"text":"ये तु धर्ममसूयन्ते बुद्धिमोहान्विता नराः ।\nअपथा गच्छतां तेषामनुयातापि पीड्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those men deluded in understanding who find fault with dharma, travelling on wrong roads, even their follower is harmed."}},{"n":64,"text":"ये तु शिष्टाः सुनियताः श्रुतित्यागपरायणाः ।\nधर्म्यं पन्थानमारूढाः सत्यधर्मपरायणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the good, well-restrained, devoted to learning and renunciation, who have taken the righteous path and are devoted to truth and dharma,"}},{"n":65,"text":"नियच्छन्ति परां बुद्धिं शिष्टाचारान्विता नराः ।\nउपाध्यायमते युक्ताः स्थित्या धर्मार्थदर्शिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"people of good conduct, steady, bring their highest understanding under control, keeping to their teacher's teaching, seeing the aims of dharma by their steadiness."}},{"n":66,"text":"नास्तिकान्भिन्नमर्यादान्क्रूरान्पापमतौ स्थितान् ।\nत्यज ताञ्ज्ञानमाश्रित्य धार्मिकानुपसेव्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leave aside atheists, those who break the bounds, the cruel and those fixed in evil purpose, relying on knowledge and serving the righteous."}},{"n":67,"text":"कामलोभग्रहाकीर्णां पञ्चेन्द्रियजलां नदीम् ।\nनावं धृतिमयीं कृत्वा जन्मदुर्गाणि संतर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Make a boat of steadiness and cross the river full of desire and greed as crocodiles, and the five senses as its waters, and pass over the difficult places of birth."}},{"n":68,"text":"क्रमेण संचितो धर्मो बुद्धियोगमयो महान् ।\nशिष्टाचारे भवेत्साधू रागः शुक्लेव वाससि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma gathered gradually, great, made of the discipline of understanding, becomes in the conduct of the good like colour on white cloth."}},{"n":69,"text":"अहिंसा सत्यवचनं सर्वभूतहितं परम् ।\nअहिंसा परमो धर्मः स च सत्ये प्रतिष्ठितः ।\nसत्ये कृत्वा प्रतिष्ठां तु प्रवर्तन्ते प्रवृत्तयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Non-violence, truthful speech and the highest good of all beings: non-violence is the highest dharma, and it rests on truth. Having made truth the base, actions go forth."}},{"n":70,"text":"सत्यमेव गरीयस्तु शिष्टाचारनिषेवितम् ।\nआचारश्च सतां धर्मः सन्तश्चाचारलक्षणाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Truth alone is weightier, practised in the conduct of the good. Conduct is the dharma of the good, and the good are marked by conduct."}},{"n":71,"text":"यो यथाप्रकृतिर्जन्तुः स्वां स्वां प्रकृतिमश्नुते ।\nपापात्मा क्रोधकामादीन्दोषानाप्नोत्यनात्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each creature obtains its own nature according to what it is; the sinful, undisciplined man obtains faults like anger and desire."}},{"n":72,"text":"आरम्भो न्याययुक्तो यः स हि धर्म इति स्मृतः ।\nअनाचारस्त्वधर्मेति एतच्छिष्टानुशासनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The undertaking that is joined with right is called dharma; bad conduct is unrighteousness: this is the teaching of the good."}},{"n":73,"text":"अक्रुध्यन्तोऽनसूयन्तो निरहंकारमत्सराः ।\nऋजवः शमसंपन्नाः शिष्टाचारा भवन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who are not angry, not envious, without ego or jealousy, honest and endowed with calm are of the conduct of the good."}},{"n":74,"text":"त्रैविद्यवृद्धाः शुचयो वृत्तवन्तो मनस्विनः ।\nगुरुशुश्रूषवो दान्ताः शिष्टाचारा भवन्त्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The pure, elders in the three Vedas, well-behaved, thoughtful, who serve their teachers and are self-controlled, are of the conduct of the good."}},{"n":75,"text":"तेषामदीनसत्त्वानां दुष्कराचारकर्मणाम् ।\nस्वैः कर्मभिः सत्कृतानां घोरत्वं संप्रणश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those of unbroken spirit, who do hard deeds of conduct and are honoured by their own deeds, fierceness vanishes."}},{"n":76,"text":"तं सदाचारमाश्चर्यं पुराणं शाश्वतं ध्रुवम् ।\nधर्मं धर्मेण पश्यन्तः स्वर्गं यान्ति मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that wondrous, ancient, eternal and fixed good conduct, the dharma, through dharma, the wise go to heaven."}},{"n":77,"text":"आस्तिका मानहीनाश्च द्विजातिजनपूजकाः ।\nश्रुतवृत्तोपसंपन्नाः ते सन्तः स्वर्गगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Believers, free of pride, who honour the twice-born, endowed with learning and conduct, those good people go to heaven."}},{"n":78,"text":"वेदोक्तः परमो धर्मो धर्मशास्त्रेषु चापरः ।\nशिष्टाचीर्णश्च शिष्टानां त्रिविधं धर्मलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The highest dharma is that stated in the Veda; another is in the law books; and a third is what the good practise: this is the threefold mark of dharma."}},{"n":79,"text":"पारणं चापि विद्यानां तीर्थानामवगाहनम् ।\nक्षमा सत्यार्जवं शौचं शिष्टाचारनिदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Completing studies, bathing at holy places, forbearance, truth, honesty and purity are the signs of the conduct of the good."}},{"n":80,"text":"सर्वभूतदयावन्तो अहिंसानिरताः सदा ।\nपरुषं न प्रभाषन्ते सदा सन्तो द्विजप्रियाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Merciful to all beings, always devoted to non-violence, the good, dear to brahmins, never speak harshly."}},{"n":81,"text":"शुभानामशुभानां च कर्मणां फलसंचये ।\nविपाकमभिजानन्ति ते शिष्टाः शिष्टसंमताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those who understand the ripening of good and bad deeds in the gathering of their fruit are the good, approved by the good."}},{"n":82,"text":"न्यायोपेता गुणोपेताः सर्वलोकहितैषिणः ।\nसन्तः स्वर्गजितः शुक्लाः संनिविष्टाश्च सत्पथे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Possessed of justice and virtues, wishing well to all the world, the good, pure, who have conquered heaven, are set on the good path."}},{"n":83,"text":"दातारः संविभक्तारो दीनानुग्रहकारिणः ।\nसर्वभूतदयावन्तस्ते शिष्टाः शिष्टसंमताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Givers, sharers, those who help the poor and are merciful to all beings are the good, approved by the good."}},{"n":84,"text":"सर्वपूज्याः श्रुतधनास्तथैव च तपस्विनः ।\nदाननित्याः सुखाँल्लोकानाप्नुवन्तीह च श्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Honoured by all, rich in learning and also ascetics, always giving, they obtain happy worlds and prosperity here."}},{"n":85,"text":"पीडया च कलत्रस्य भृत्यानां च समाहिताः ।\nअतिशक्त्या प्रयच्छन्ति सन्तः सद्भिः समागताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking pains over their wives and servants, they give beyond their means, the good who have joined the good."}},{"n":86,"text":"लोकयात्रां च पश्यन्तो धर्ममात्महितानि च ।\nएवं सन्तो वर्तमाना एधन्ते शाश्वतीः समाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looking at the course of the world, at dharma and their own good, the good who live thus flourish for endless years."}},{"n":87,"text":"अहिंसा सत्यवचनमानृशंस्यमथार्जवम् ।\nअद्रोहो नातिमानश्च ह्रीस्तितिक्षा दमः शमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Non-violence, truthful speech, kindness, honesty, freedom from malice, freedom from excess pride, modesty, patience, self-restraint and calm,"}},{"n":88,"text":"धीमन्तो धृतिमन्तश्च भूतानामनुकम्पकाः ।\nअकामद्वेषसंयुक्तास्ते सन्तो लोकसत्कृताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"the wise, steady and compassionate to beings, free of desire and hatred: these are the good honoured by the world."}},{"n":89,"text":"त्रीण्येव तु पदान्याहुः सतां वृत्तमनुत्तमम् ।\nन द्रुह्येच्चैव दद्याच्च सत्यं चैव सदा वदेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They say there are three steps in the best conduct of the good: do not harm, give, and always speak truth."}},{"n":90,"text":"सर्वत्र च दयावन्तः सन्तः करुणवेदिनः ।\nगच्छन्तीह सुसंतुष्टा धर्म्यं पन्थानमुत्तमम् ।\nशिष्टाचारा महात्मानो येषां धर्मः सुनिश्चितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The good, compassionate everywhere and knowing mercy, content, walk here the best path of dharma; the great-souled of good conduct have dharma well settled."}},{"n":91,"text":"अनसूया क्षमा शान्तिः संतोषः प्रियवादिता ।\nकामक्रोधपरित्यागः शिष्टाचारनिषेवणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freedom from envy, patience, peace, contentment, pleasant speech, giving up desire and anger, and practising the conduct of the good."}},{"n":92,"text":"कर्मणा श्रुतसंपन्नं सतां मार्गमनुत्तमम् ।\nशिष्टाचारं निषेवन्ते नित्यं धर्मेष्वतन्द्रिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Always unwearied in dharma, they follow in deed the best path of the good, which is rich in learning and the conduct of the good."}},{"n":93,"text":"प्रज्ञाप्रासादमारुह्य मुह्यतो महतो जनान् ।\nप्रेक्षन्तो लोकवृत्तानि विविधानि द्विजोत्तम ।\nअतिपुण्यानि पापानि तानि द्विजवरोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Climbing the palace of wisdom, they look on the many conducts of the world and on the great multitude who are bewildered, best of brahmins, and on their very meritorious and sinful acts."}},{"n":94,"text":"एतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं यथाप्रज्ञं यथाश्रुतम् ।\nशिष्टाचारगुणान्ब्रह्मन्पुरस्कृत्य द्विजर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this has been told to you as I understand it and as I heard it, brahmin, putting forward the virtues of the conduct of the good, bull among brahmins."}}]}]}